{"sounds":{"intro":"Old Church Slavonic is the oldest written Slavic language, created in the 9th century by the brothers Cyril and Methodius for the Slavs of Moravia. It was first written in Glagolitic, then in Cyrillic, which is what is used here. It is the ancestor of Russian, Bulgarian, Serbian and others, and the liturgical language of many Orthodox churches. The pronunciation is reconstructed.","rows":[["ѣ","like \"ya\" in \"yard\", or a long \"e\"","вѣра"],["ѫ","a nasal \"o\", like French \"on\"","рѫка"],["ѧ","a nasal \"e\", like French \"in\"","пѧть"],["ъ / ь","very short vowels, \"oo\" and \"ee\", dropped in later Slavic languages","домъ"],["ы","like \"i\" in \"bit\" said further back","рыба"],["щ","\"sht\"","нощь"]],"notes":["Nouns have seven cases, three genders and singular, dual and plural. Many masculine nouns end in -ъ: домъ, градъ, богъ.","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. Only well-attested words and forms are included. The pronunciation is reconstructed and nothing has been checked by a specialist, so treat it as a first guide."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","единъ","EH-dee-noo"],["two","дъва","DOO-vah"],["three","трьє","TREE-yeh"],["four","четыре","cheh-TIH-reh"],["five","пѧть","PEHN-tee"],["six","шесть","SHES-tee"],["seven","седмь","SED-mee"],["eight","осмь","OS-mee"],["nine","девѧть","DEH-vehn-tee"],["ten","десѧть","DEH-sehn-tee"]]},{"id":"bigger-numbers","title":"Bigger numbers","items":[["one hundred","съто","SOO-toh"],["one thousand","тысѧшти","tih-SEHN-shtee"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"greetings","title":"Greetings","items":[["rejoice / hail","радуисѧ","RAH-doo-ee-sehn"],["peace be with you","миръ вамъ","meer vahm"],["thanks","благодарѧ","blah-goh-DAH-rehn"],["have mercy","помилуи","poh-MEE-loo-ee"],["yes","ей","ay"],["no","нѣ","nyeh"],["glory","слава","SLAH-vah"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"about-me","title":"About me","items":[["I","азъ","AH-zoo"],["you (one)","ты","tih"],["he","онъ","OH-noo"],["she","она","oh-NAH"],["we","мы","mih"],["you (many)","вы","vih"],["they","они","oh-NEE"],["I am","есмь","ES-mee"],["you are","еси","EH-see"],["he is","естъ","ES-too"],["I know","вѣмь","VYEH-mee"],["I do not know","не вѣмь","neh VYEH-mee"],["what?","чьто","CHEE-toh"],["who?","къто","KOO-toh"],["where?","къде","KOO-deh"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and family","items":[["father","отьць","OH-teets"],["mother","мати","MAH-tee"],["son","сынъ","SIH-noo"],["daughter","дъшти","DOO-shtee"],["brother","братръ","BRAH-troo"],["sister","сестра","seh-STRAH"],["man","мѫжь","MOHN-zhee"],["woman","жена","zheh-NAH"],["child","дѣтѧ","DYEH-tehn"],["king / emperor","цѣсарь","TSYEH-sah-ree"],["god","богъ","boh-GOO"],["lord","господь","GOH-spoh-dee"]]},{"id":"nature-and-things","title":"Nature and things","items":[["sun","слъньце","SLOON-tseh"],["moon","мѣсѧць","MYEH-sehn-ts"],["star","звѣзда","zvyeh-ZDAH"],["sky","небо","NEH-boh"],["earth","землѧ","ZEH-mlyah"],["water","вода","voh-DAH"],["fire","огнь","OH-gnee"],["city","градъ","grah-DOO"],["mountain","гора","goh-RAH"],["tree","дрѣво","DRYEH-voh"],["bread","хлѣбъ","hlyeh-BOO"],["wine","вино","VEE-noh"],["fish","рыба","RIH-bah"],["dog","пьсъ","PEE-soo"],["wolf","влъкъ","vloo-KOO"],["house","домъ","doh-MOO"],["day","дьнь","DEE-nee"],["night","нощь","nohshch"],["name","имѧ","EE-mehn"],["word","слово","SLOH-voh"]]},{"id":"body","title":"Body","items":[["hand","рѫка","ROHN-kah"],["foot","нога","noh-GAH"],["eye","око","OH-koh"],["ear","ухо","OO-hoh"],["heart","срьдьце","SEER-deeh-tseh"],["head","глава","glah-VAH"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["good","добръ","DOH-broo"],["bad / evil","зълъ","ZOO-loo"],["big / great","великъ","veh-LEE-koo"],["small","малъ","mah-LOO"],["new","новъ","noh-VOO"],["old","старъ","stah-ROO"],["white","бѣлъ","byeh-LOO"],["black","чьрнъ","CHEER-noo"]]},{"id":"verbs-to-do","title":"Verbs (to do)","items":[["to be","быти","BIH-tee"],["to eat","ѣсти","YEH-stee"],["to drin